where the Muses,
meeting Thamyris the Thracian, stopped him from song
as he was going from Oechalia, from Eurytus the Oechalian;

And of the Aetolians was leading Thoas, son of Andraemon,
who inhabited Pleuron and Olenus and Pylene,
and Chalcis near the sea and Calydon, rocky;

And Tlepolemus, when then he had been reared in the well-framed hall,
at once his own father’s dear mother’s-brother killed,
already growing old, Licymnius, scion of Ares;
